data: {"level":2,"reviewed":{"level":2,"label":"formula / approach","text":"Training: $\\mu_B$ is the mean over rows, $\\sigma_B^2$ is the variance over rows with divisor $N$, and $y=\\gamma\\,\\frac{x-\\mu_B}{\\sqrt{\\sigma_B^2+\\epsilon}}+\\beta$. The running variance is updated with the same batch variance rescaled by $\\frac{N}{N-1}$. In both running updates, the new batch statistic is weighted by momentum. Inference uses the stored statistics in the same $y$ formula."},"hints_note":null}

